$DATUM 4-formylbenzoic acid (71 mg, 473 μmol), 4,9-Dioxa-1,12-dodecanediamine
(44 mg, 215 μmol), N,N’-Dicyclohexylcarbodiimide (97 mg, 471 μmol), and
HOBt (72 mg, 470 μmol) were added to CH2Cl2 (12 mL) at 0 ºC. After
stirring for 2 h, the solution was filtered and evaporated with stream of
nitrogen gas. The product was then dissolved in 20 mL of 50 %
acetonitrile and 0.1 % trifluoroacetic acid and was purified by RP-HPLC.
1 (76 mg, 76 %). 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 10.07 (s, 2H), 8.66-8.64 (t,
2H), 8.02-7.98 (m, 8H), 3.43-3.32 (m, 12H), 1.79-1.74 (quin, 4H),
1.55-1.53 (quin, 4H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 192.87, 165.30,
139.64, 137.64, 129.35, 127.84, 69.84, 67.77, 36.84, 29.26, 26.05.
